</name><name><surname>Roland</surname><given-names>P.</given-names></name><name><surname>Bohm</surname><given-names>C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Greitz</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Stone-Elander</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name></person-group> (<year>1990</year>). <article-title>Motor learning in man: a positron emission tomography study</article-title>. <source>Neuroreport</source> <volume>1</volume>, <fpage>57</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>60</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2129858</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tootell</surname><given-names>R. B. H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Hadjikhani</surname><given-names>N. K.</given-names></name><name><surname>Mendola</surname><given-names>J. D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Marrett</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Dale</surname><given-names>A. M.</given-names></name></person-group> (<year>1998</year>). <article-title>From retinotopy to recognition: fMRI in human visual cortex</article-title>. <source>Trends Cogn. Sci.</source> <volume>2</volume>, <fpage>61</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>201</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S1364-6613(98)01171-1</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>